# Testimonial Platform — Root Environment Quick Reference
#
# This monorepo has TWO apps, each with its own `.env`:
#
#   ├── frontend/.env        — Vite build-time env (VITE_* vars only)
#   └── backend/.env         — Node.js runtime env
#
# Copy the per-app `.env.example` files into place:
#
#   cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
#   cp backend/.env.example  backend/.env
#
# Then fill in the placeholders using the explanations below.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# =============  frontend/.env  ================================================
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL
#   Base URL the React SPA uses to call the backend.
#   Local:  http://localhost:5000/api/v1
#   Vercel: paste your Render backend base URL, e.g.
#             https://testimonial-api-abc12.onrender.com/api/v1
#   Note:   VITE_* vars are INLINED at build time by Vite. Every time you
#           change this on Vercel, you must re-deploy the frontend.

# =============  backend/.env  ================================================
#
# PORT
#   Local dev: 5000. Render injects its own $PORT at runtime (typically 10000);
#   server.ts reads `process.env.PORT` so no action needed.
#
# NODE_ENV
#   development | production. Render sets this automatically.
#
# MONGO_URI  (REQUIRED)
#   MongoDB Atlas +srv connection string:
#     mongodb+srv://<user>:<pass>@<cluster>.mongodb.net/testimonials?retryWrites=true&w=majority
#   Atlas → Network Access: either allow 0.0.0.0/0, or allow-list the
#   static outbound IPs from Render if you're on a paid plan.
#
# CORS_ORIGINS
#   Comma-separated list of origins that may call this backend:
#     CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,https://testimonial-app.vercel.app
#   Or set `CORS_ORIGINS=*` in staging.
#
# CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME / CLOUDINARY_API_KEY / CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET
#   Reserved for future photo upload pipeline. Safe to leave as placeholders.
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY  (optional)
#   Google AI Studio API key. Leave blank or = DISABLED to run without AI.
#   When provided, every submission is fire-and-forget analysed for
#   sentiment / confidence / AI summary. Failures never block submissions.
